                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_cv.png" id="497-0" width=27 height=27 alt="continuously variable pattern selection" title="Continuously variable pattern selection"></span>Chameleon Labs TS-2</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The TS-2 is a large-diaphragm multipattern tube mic. Like its SDC brother (Chameleon&#8217;s TS-1), the TS-2 was designed by and named for <a href="http://www.evergreen.edu/faculty/sfaculty.htm#settert">Terry Setter</a>, a faculty member of Evergreen State College and occasional writer for TapeOp.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s one-inch capsule has two diaphragms; a switch on the power supply allows selection of an infinite number of polar patterns ranging from omni to figure-8. </p><p>We have received conflicting data about the mic&#8217;s capsule, but based on its source we believe it to be a 34mm capsule with 27mm diaphragms. The diaphragm thickness is 3 microns.</p><p>Like the TS-1, the TS-2 is manufactured in China, using locally-sourced parts &#8212; with the exception of a single &#8220;exotic&#8221; capacitor, used as the final decoupling cap before the transformer. Chameleon provides this capacitor to the Chinese factory.</p><p>Also like the TS-1, the TS-2 includes an over-engineered tube power supply, designed by Terry Setter. It provides a unique feature: the heater voltage is controllable by the user, allowing the mic&#8217;s character or warmth to be adjusted to best complement the source &#8212; at a cost of potentially overdriving the vacuum tube.</p><p>Included:</p><ul><li>TS-2 Microphone</li><li>Dedicated power supply</li><li>25&#39; 7-pin power cable</li><li>Suspension shockmount</li><li>Aluminum case</li><li>windscreen</li></ul><p>The TS-2 can be special ordered with a hand-selected tube (rather than the Chinese 12AT7). Chameleon Labs also offers &#8220;circuit changes to enhance [the mic&#8217;s] sonic character for discriminating users.&#8221;<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Chameleon-Labs/TS-2">Chameleon Labs TS-2</a> is also known as: TS2.</p>
